{
    "upload_type": "software",
    "title": "echemdb metadata-schema",
    "description": "<p>Metadata schemas for describing electrochemical systems and the collected data, developed within the <a href=\"https://www.echemdb.org\">echemdb</a> community project. The repository contains</p><ul><li>the schemas defined in <a href=\"https://linkml.io\">LinkML</a> (<code>linkml/</code>), the single source of truth,</li><li>the JSON Schemas generated from them (<code>schemas/</code>), which can be used to validate metadata in any language or tool that supports JSON Schema,</li><li>example and template metadata files (<code>examples/</code>), and</li><li>the <code>mdstools</code> Python package to flatten, enrich, validate and migrate metadata files.</li></ul><p>A new version is archived for every release. Changes between versions are listed in the <a href=\"https://github.com/echemdb/metadata-schema/blob/main/ChangeLog\">ChangeLog</a>.</p>",
